# Copy to .env (Git-ignored, mode 0600) beside docker-compose.yml. Compose
# passes it to the container and reads the host entries at the end.
# Never commit real values.
# Any OpenAI-compatible base URL and its API key (CLIProxyAPI is one option).
# The key may stay empty for a local server that needs no key.
EPHEMERA_UPSTREAM_BASE_URL=
EPHEMERA_UPSTREAM_API_KEY=
# Optional: on (the default) sends each call's cache key as body
# prompt_cache_key and header x-session-affinity; an upstream that refuses
# them by name stops getting them by itself. off never sends them.
EPHEMERA_UPSTREAM_SESSION_CACHE=
# Optional: the model new libraries start with for replies, as the provider
# lists it; each person can change it in the app. Empty: everyone chooses on
# first use.
EPHEMERA_DEFAULT_MODEL=
# At least 32 random characters, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`; the trusted
# authentication proxy sends it.
EPHEMERA_PROXY_KEY=
# Optional: the key of Atelier (an optional ComfyUI backend) for creating a
# character from an image, at least 32 random characters and different from
# EPHEMERA_PROXY_KEY. It opens that one route only; leave it empty to turn the
# integration off.
EPHEMERA_INTEGRATION_KEY=
# The master key every user's data is encrypted under: 32 random bytes as 64 hex
# characters, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`. Required. Losing it loses every user's
# data for good, and nothing can recover it: back it up somewhere safe yourself.
# A different key fails the start.
EPHEMERA_DATA_KEY=
# Exact browser origin, e.g. https://ephemera.example.
EPHEMERA_ORIGIN=
# Optional, for card portraits: the bearer token of the ComfyUI set in Settings
# (Atelier requires one), passed to the container as is.
COMFYUI_API_KEY=
# The only ComfyUI origins Settings may name, comma-separated (e.g.
# https://comfyui.example:8188); empty turns portraits off for every user.
COMFYUI_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=
# Optional: the workflow a new user starts with and a vanished choice falls
# back to (krea2-gonzalomo by default); it must have a graph.
EPHEMERA_DEFAULT_WORKFLOW=
# Optional: more ComfyUI node classes server files and imported workflows may
# use, comma-separated (at most 200). Listing a class means you vouch that it
# keeps its output in memory; save and preview nodes are always refused, and
# naming one stops the start.
EPHEMERA_COMFYUI_EXTRA_NODES=
# Optional: on (the default) adds the bundled example character to each new
# user's library once; off starts new libraries empty.
EPHEMERA_STARTER_CHARACTER=
# Optional: EPHEMERA_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS (600000). The Compose file fixes
# EPHEMERA_HOST, EPHEMERA_STATIC_DIR and the container's data path; leave
# EPHEMERA_PORT unset (the published port maps to the default 8790).

# Host only: the data directory, ideally on an encrypted volume.
EPHEMERA_DATA_DIR=
# Host only, optional: the PEM CA certificate ComfyUI's TLS certificate chains
# to. Compose binds it read-only and points the container at its copy.
COMFYUI_CA_FILE=
# Host only, optional: a directory of more ComfyUI workflow graphs (`<id>.json`,
# and `<id>.reference.json` for a reference graph). Compose binds it read-only
# and points the container at its copy, read once at startup beside the bundled
# graphs and offered to every user, at most 64 workflows in all. A graph may
# carry a top-level "ephemera": {"family": "krea2" | "moss" | "general",
# "name": "..."} key. A file named like another, or starting with the reserved
# `user-` prefix, stops the start. Users import their own in Settings.
EPHEMERA_WORKFLOWS_DIR=
